PERMITTED USE

You may fork, clone, and study the source code in this repository for
personal, educational, or non-commercial purposes. You may use the
underlying code patterns, architecture, and technical approach as a
reference or starting point to build your own original portfolio or
personal website, provided that your project does not replicate the
visual design, branding, or identity described below.

RESTRICTIONS

The following elements are proprietary and may NOT be copied, reused,
redistributed, or included in derivative works without prior written
permission from the copyright holder:

1. Visual design: page layouts, color schemes, typography
   combinations, UI component styling, animations, transitions,
   and the overall look and feel of the site as presented at
   scalewithalap.com.

2. Brand assets: the "Scale with Alap" name, logos, icons, favicons,
   illustrations, photographs, screenshots, and any other graphic
   files included in the public/ directory or any project asset folders.

3. Personal content: biographical text, project descriptions,
   resume data, testimonials, and any copy written specifically
   for Alap Putatunda's portfolio.

4. Commercial use: using this code, in whole or in part, to build
   a product or service that is sold, licensed, or monetized in
   any form without separate written agreement.

IN SHORT

- Want to learn from the code and build something that looks and
  feels like your own? Go ahead.

- Want to ship a site that looks like a copy of scalewithalap.com,
  or use my name and assets as if they were yours? Don't.

